Use precisely exists_isPrimeTriangle hypotheses: E is stably unramified CM,
embedded in Q(mu_N), N+t<y, four or more infinite places,
gamma in G_E, and (chi(gamma)^a-1) divides ell^h for 0<a<t,
ell<=y^2 or h=0, and the stated shifted mostFrobeniiAt condition W.
Write q=chi(gamma), C=ell^(yh), P_e=prod_{0<=k<t,k!=e}(q^e-q^k).
For e>k, q^e-q^k=q^k(q^(e-k)-1); for k>e exchange signs.
Every difference divides ell^h because q is a unit. Hence
 P_e | ell^((t-1)h) (when t>0).
For 0<e<t let D_e=q^e-1. Native four_dvd_cycChar_sub_one
applies to gamma^e, hence 4|D_e even at ell=2 (retain its
stably-unramified root-of-unity hypothesis). Thus
 4 D_e^2 P_e | D_e^3 P_e | ell^((t+2)h) | C.
Here t+2<=y follows from N>=1 and N+t<y. This is the exact
hD/h2 stronger payment before reduction modulo ell^nu.
It implies both P_e|C and 4D_e^2|C without dividing by
any character difference or by 2. For t=0 the family and
product conditions are vacuous, and for t=1 there are no
positive twists. For h=0 the cost product is zero even if
