We retain this exact count as a prerequisite of this paragraph.
Let R=Z/ell^nu and m=|iota|. By elementary divisors for the finite
R-module Y, its minimal generator number is d=log_ell |Y[ell]|.
The evaluation image in R^m is generated by at most d elements.
Adjoin the k requested zero vectors pi(res(y_i)^-1).
The resulting submodule of R^m has at most d+k<=m-1 generators.
Lift its generators to columns over Z_ell. Smith normal form
of the resulting m by (d+k) matrix gives a primitive row n
