 r(u)=m^(t-1)*prod_{a!=e}(m^e-m^a)*r(w) in R.
Thus r(u) is a unit multiple of the image of P_e, with
m and r(w) units; 4 r(u)|C in R by section 1.
The statement is valid also when that product is zero in R;
